Sometimes you need to navigate in code (e.g., after a form submission). Inject the `Router` service and call `navigate()`.

```typescript
import { Router } from '@angular/router';

constructor(private router: Router) {}

goToProduct(id: number) {
  this.router.navigate(['/products', id]);
}
```

* `navigate()` takes an array of path segments (like `routerLink`).
* `navigateByUrl('/products/42')` takes a complete URL string.

Both return a Promise that resolves when navigation succeeds.
